#edb/ref 17592186050379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429466 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429467 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429468 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429469 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429470 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429471 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429472 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429473 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429474 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429475 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429476 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429477 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429478 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429479 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429480 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1031 "Integrating Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1033 478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1034 1.4445686090904644 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050489 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4d6f30e9-3dde-50ef-bfb2-830878d94eaf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186547791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094735 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "10bf188f-45f0-56ee-9364-6499de462127" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096479 #edb/ref 1069 "e-499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096479 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int (x^4-3x) \\cos(x) \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096479 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4bca758-9903-505c-9828-0e1788b25d9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096479 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral we choose $u = x^4-3x$ and $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\cos(x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^4-3x$ | $\\cos(x)$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} 4x^3-3$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} \\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} (x^4-3x)\\sin(x)$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 12x^2$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}   -\\cos(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}  -(4x^3-3)(-\\cos(x))$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} 24x$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1}  -\\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 12x^2(-\\sin(x))$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1} 24$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} \\cos(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1}- 24x\\cos(x)$ |\n| $0$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1}  \\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1}+$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1}  24\\sin(x)$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{4}-3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =({x}^{4}-3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+(4{x}^{3}-3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & \\,\\,-12{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-24x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C \\\\  & =({x}^{4}-12{x}^{2}-3x+24)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & \\,\\,+(4{x}^{3}-24x-3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096482 #edb/ref 1069 "e-500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096482 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int (x^2-1)(x+2)^5 \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096482 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "96f1c791-f1cd-5a20-a6ee-004475bbd482" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096482 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral, we choose $u = x^2-1$ and $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x} =(x+2)^5.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^2-1$ | $(x+2)^5$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} 2x$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\\dfrac{(x+2)^6}{6}$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\\dfrac{(x^2-1)(x+2)^6}{6}$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 2$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} \\dfrac{(x+2)^7}{42}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -\\,\\dfrac{x(x+2)^7}{21}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\\dfrac{(x+2)^8}{336}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1}  \\dfrac{(x+2)^8}{168}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}-1)(x+2)^{5}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)(x+2)^{6}}{6}-\\frac{x(x+2)^{7}}{21}+\\frac{(x+2)^{8}}{168}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)^{6}}{168}(28({x}^{2}-1)-8x(x+2)+(x+2)^{2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)^{6}}{168}(21{x}^{2}-12x-24)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186547979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186548028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186548032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186548035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186548067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1039 "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096680 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7ffce8b3-cc12-5a4d-88fd-77889b6bdd3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186547973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186547976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186548049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186548060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1039 "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096681 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1045 "The Tabular Method of Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1050 840.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096911 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "5599d88c-65b1-5f17-bfd1-cbd036adf9c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097127 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186094735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097127 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097127 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097127 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate  $\\int (4{x}^{4}+2){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097127 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89395e95-1dd7-5374-9986-857a303ac379" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097127 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral, we choose $u=4{x}^{4}+2$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4{x}^{4}+2$ | ${e}^{x}$ |  |  |\n| $16{x}^{3}$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $+$ | $(4{x}^{4}+2){e}^{x}$ |\n| $48{x}^{2}$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $-$ | $-16{x}^{3}{e}^{x}$ |\n| $96x$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $+$ | $48{x}^{2}{e}^{x}$ |\n| $96$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $-$ | $-96x{e}^{x}$ |\n| $0$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $+$ | $96{e}^{x}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{4}+2){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={e}^{x}(4{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-96x+98)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097530 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097530 #edb/ref 1061 1760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097530 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a907607b-33d6-5787-9f76-4ba49a6d4daf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097530 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097531 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097531 #edb/ref 1061 1761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097531 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2713bc66-d154-57b0-a43a-a25388531743" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097531 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097532 #edb/ref 1061 1765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097532 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ba6ae8dc-2771-5af3-981d-bd894fac5705" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097532 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097928 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int x^3e^{x/2} \\textrm{d}x.$ We can do it by applying integration by parts three times, but the calculation is pretty long. How can we speed it up?\n\nMultiple applications of integration by parts become quick and easy if we use the **tabular method**.\n\nLet's start by picking our $u$ and $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}$ as normal:\n\n$$\nu = x^3\\,,\\quad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x} = e^{x/2}\\,.\n$$\n\nWe put this in a table, as shown below:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same Color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^3$ | $e^{x/2}$ |  |  |\n\nTo fill in the second row of the table, we differentiate the function in the first column and integrate the function in the second column. Doing this, we find\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(x^3\\right) = 3x^2\\,,\\quad \\int e^{x/2} \\textrm{d}x = 2e^{x/2}\\,.\n$$\n\nFilling in our table, we get the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same Color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^3$ | $e^{x/2}$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} 3x^2$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}2e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ |  |\n\nAt this step, we begin filling the third column. It always starts with a \"$+$\" and then the signs alternate at each subsequent step.\n\nWe continue by differentiating the expression in the first column and integrating the expression in the second column until we get zero in the first column.\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same Color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}  x^3$ | $e^{x/2}$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} 3x^2$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}2e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 6x$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}  4e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,0}$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} 6$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 8e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1}16e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1}$ |\n\nNow we multiply the same-colored terms along with the same-colored sign. Specifically we multiply $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^3$ with ${\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} 2e^{x/2}},$ $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}3x^2$ with $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}4e^{x/2},$ and so on. We get\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same Color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}  x^3$ | $e^{x/2}$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}3x^2$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}2e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} 2x^3e^{x/2}$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 6x$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}  4e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}  -12x^2e^{x/2}$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} 6$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 8e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 48xe^{x/2}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1}16e^{x/2}$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} -96e^{x/2}$ |\n\nFinally, we add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3}{e}^{x/2}\\text{d}x & =2{x}^{3}{e}^{x/2}-12{x}^{2}{e}^{x/2}+48x{e}^{x/2}-96{e}^{x/2}+C \\\\  & ={e}^{x/2}(2{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+48x-96)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097928 #edb/ref 1065 907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097928 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ce8fcadc-c0d9-53c8-93f1-7c7946d0ec31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097928 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547316 #edb/ref 1080 "-(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547316 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547316 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "005d8792-e152-5779-a4e7-ff8164391a13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547329 #edb/ref 1080 "(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}+124)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}+(24{x}^{3}-16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547329 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547329 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05134a4e-1d46-5e28-bcb2-8f6817ff28b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547332 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}+32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547332 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547332 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "076b789d-51b5-5ef9-a0dd-ba86934844f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547335 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}+32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}+12x+3)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547335 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547335 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08b769a9-d021-5cbd-b502-3820d8cbbf8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547340 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{x}(4{x}^{4}+16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-96x+98)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547340 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547340 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b88c051-a025-5f03-81cf-5494a62f33da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547350 #edb/ref 1080 "({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-6x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x