92186547976 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\int (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547976 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1051456d-d936-5dd0-8e18-6d4a40dca9fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547976 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5$ | ${e}^{2x}$ |  |  |\n| $6{x}^{2}+6x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x}}{2}$ |\n| $12x+6$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+3x){e}^{2x}}{2}$ |\n| $12$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{8}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(6x+3){e}^{2x}}{4}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3{e}^{2x}}{4}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}[2(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)-2(3{x}^{2}+3x)+(6x+3)-3]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}(4{x}^{3}+10)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{3}+5)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547979 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547979 #edb/ref 1069 "q-51229" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547979 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547979 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\int ({x}^{3}+x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547979 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1627a960-4b89-5682-9e7a-8ebccade355e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547979 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral we choose $u={x}^{3}+x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{3}+x$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ |  |  |\n| $3{x}^{2}+1$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ | $+$ | $({x}^{3}+x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ |\n| $6x$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}$ | $-$ | $(3{x}^{2}+1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n| $6$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}$ | $+$ | $-\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{3}+x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =({x}^{3}+x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+(3{x}^{2}+1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C \\\\  & =(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548028 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548028 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14755" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548028 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548028 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\int (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548028 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8eec90d6-f38c-50f0-b171-7f37a87f27a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548028 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same Color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ |  |  |\n| $6{x}^{2}+6x$ | $-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ | $+$ | $-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ |\n| $12x+6$ | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ | $-$ | $(6{x}^{2}+6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ |\n| $12$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ | $+$ | $(12x+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ |\n| $0$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ | $-$ | $-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(6{x}^{2}+6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(12x+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C \\\\  & =-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-12x-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(6{x}^{2}+6x-12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548032 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548032 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104069" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548032 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548032 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int 2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548032 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "98841fb8-b49b-5f0b-816e-9b78835d046c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548032 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral we choose $u=2{x}^{3}$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{3}$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ |  |  |\n| $6{x}^{2}$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}$ | $+$ | $-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ |\n| $12x$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}$ | $-$ | $\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ |\n| $12$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C \\\\  & =(3x-2{x}^{3})\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+(6{x}^{2}-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548035 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548035 #edb/ref 1069 "q-13148" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548035 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548035 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int ({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548035 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9ecd3f37-138d-5c59-a588-9da4d5939fe0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548035 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral we choose $u={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ |  |  |\n| $3{x}^{2}+6x$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ |\n| $6x+6$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}$ | $-$ | $\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n| $6$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}$ | $+$ | $-\\frac{(3x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{(3x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C \\\\  & =(2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-3x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}+12x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548049 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548049 #edb/ref 1069 "q-13147" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548049 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548049 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\int (2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548049 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c451ec1c-6a2b-54c4-80d7-187b41f5f298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548049 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{4}+4x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{4}+4x$ | ${e}^{3x}$ |  |  |\n| $8{x}^{3}+4$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}}{3}$ |\n| $24{x}^{2}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{(8{x}^{3}+4){e}^{3x}}{9}$ |\n| $48x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{27}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{8{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{9}$ |\n| $48$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{16x{e}^{3x}}{27}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{243}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{16{e}^{3x}}{81}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}(27(2{x}^{4}+4x)-9(8{x}^{3}+4)+9(8{x}^{2})-3(16x)+16)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{3}+72{x}^{2}+60x-20)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{81}(27{x}^{4}-36{x}^{3}+36{x}^{2}+30x-10)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548060 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14773" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548060 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548060 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int 2{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548060 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d35b604c-10fb-5e20-9163-ae0fba981c99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548060 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{4}$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{4}$ | ${e}^{4x}$ |  |  |\n| $8{x}^{3}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}}{2}$ |\n| $24{x}^{2}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{{x}^{3}{e}^{4x}}{2}$ |\n| $48x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{3{x}^{2}{e}^{4x}}{8}$ |\n| $48$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{256}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{16}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{1024}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{64}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\int 2{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}-32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548067 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548067 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14779" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548067 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548067 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate  $\\int (2{x}^{4}+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548067 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3b2de25-1eea-5c88-bd03-1de1fe67ccfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548067 #edb/ref 1074 "For this integral we choose $u=2{x}^{4}+4$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{4}+4$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ |  |  |\n| $8{x}^{3}$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(2{x}^{4}+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}$ |\n| $24{x}^{2}$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}$ | $-$ | $\\frac{8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}$ |\n| $48x$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{27}$ | $+$ | $-\\frac{8{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}$ |\n| $48$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{81}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{16x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{243}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{4}+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(2{x}^{4}+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{8{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{16x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+\\frac{16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}+C \\\\  & =(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}+124)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}+(24{x}^{3}-16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
